# Local overrides — values here take precedence over opengym.env.
# Copy to opengym.override.env, fill in, then symlink. Gitignored: this file
# carries the real hostname and your admin user id.

# ── Required: the public hostname ──────────────────────────────────────────
# RP_ID is a BARE hostname: no scheme, no port, no trailing slash.
# ORIGIN is the full URL, and must match the browser's address bar exactly.
#
# Settle these before anyone registers. Passkeys are bound to the exact
# hostname, so changing RP_ID later invalidates every existing passkey and
# everyone has to register again.
#RP_ID=gym.example.com
#ORIGIN=https://gym.example.com

# ── Step 1 of the bootstrap: uncomment to register the first profile ───────
# opengym.env ships INVITE_ONLY=1, and an invite code can only be generated from
# the admin dashboard — which needs an admin, which needs a registered user. So
# open signup just long enough to create your own profile:
#INVITE_ONLY=0

# ── Step 2: make yourself admin, then delete the line above ────────────────
# Your id is in ~opengym/data/db.json under users[].id. Comma-separated for
# several admins. Then `systemctl --user restart opengym-api` and confirm the
# Admin dashboard link appears in Settings.
#ADMIN_UIDS=

# ── Optional ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Contact address sent with push notifications; defaults to your ORIGIN.
#VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.com
